verses.text:
For we sinned and did lawlessly in departing from you,
and we sinned in everything,
and to the commandments of your law we did not listen;

And you handed us over into the hands of lawless enemies,
most hateful apostates,
and to a king unjust and the most wicked in all the earth.{b}

And now it is not for us to open our mouth;
shame and reproach have come to your slaves
and to those who worship you.

to whom you spoke, saying that you would multiply their seed
as the stars of heaven
and as the sand that is on the shore of the sea.{c}

And there is not at this time ruler and prophet and leader,
nor whole burnt offering nor sacrifice nor offering nor incense,
nor a place to bring first fruits before you and find mercy.{d}

as with whole burnt offerings of rams and bulls
and as with ten thousands of fat lambs;
so let our sacrifice be before you today
and be fully accomplished behind you,{f}
for there is no shame for those who trust in you.

And let all who show evil to your slaves be turned back,
and let them be put to shame, stripped of all power,
and let their strength be crushed;

Bless the Lord, Hananiah, Azariah, Mishael;{m}
hymn him and exalt him above all to the ages;
for he has drawn us out of Hades
and saved us from the hand of death
and rescued us from the midst of the burning flame
and from the midst of the fire he rescued us.

Bless, all you who revere the Lord, the God of gods;
hymn him and give thanks,
for his mercy is to the ages.{o}
